# Dienogest + 10 NMP (N-Methyl-2-pyrrolidone): XTB2 MD, spherical confinement
# Analogous to Dienogest/DMSO/Dienogest_10DMSO_MD.inp,
# Dienogest/DMF/Dienogest_10DMF_MD.inp, and
# Dienogest/MeOH/Dienogest_10MeOH_MD.inp.
#
# Starting geometry: Dienogest = the r2SCAN-3c-level gas-phase optimized
#   geometry (Dienogest/Gas/DienogestGasOptFreq.xyz, converged), same as
#   used for the MeOH build. Centroid = (-5.521, 1.467, -0.724); max
#   atom-centroid distance = 6.24 Ang.
# NMP molecules: replaced with the r2SCAN-3c/CPCM-optimized monomer geometry
#   obtained from NMP/r2SCAN3c/Monomer_r2SCAN3c_CPCM.out; position and
#   orientation of each molecule are retained from the original shell.
#   Each molecule is placed with its carbonyl O atom
#   (the primary H-bond acceptor site) on the same 12-direction sphere-shell
#   pattern used throughout this project, rotated so the molecule's bulk
#   points radially outward. NMP's own extent from its O reference atom =
#   4.32 Ang (larger than DMSO's 3.78 Ang and similar to DMF's 4.31 Ang).
# 10 NMP molecules placed at offset 11.0 Ang from Dienogest's centroid
#   (slightly larger than the 10.0 Ang used for DMSO/DMF/MeOH, since NMP is
#   a bigger molecule).
# Cell Sphere radius set to 17.0 Ang (larger than DMF's 16.0 Ang for the
#   same reason).
# Checked: min NMP-Dienogest atom distance = 5.21 Ang (no clash), max atom
#   distance from the sphere center = 15.26 Ang (safely inside the 17.0 Ang
#   sphere). Total atom count = 208 (48 + 10x16), verified.
#
# NOTE: no SMD/CPCM/ALPB here - this is a plain (unsolvated-continuum) XTB2
#   MD of the explicit cluster, consistent with the other Explicit10
#   confined MD runs in this project.

! XTB2 MD

%md
  Timestep 1.0_fs
  Initvel 298.15_K
  Thermostat NHC 298.15_K Timecon 20.0_fs
  Cell Sphere -5.521, 1.467, -0.724, 17.0 Spring 20
  Dump Position Stride 100 Filename "Dienogest_10NMP_XTB.xyz"
  Run 20000
end

